{
  "$comment": [
    "A FROZEN BASELINE, not a mirror of production.",
    "",
    "The migration-history reconciliation of 2026-09-19 established which",
    "migrations had been applied up to baselineThrough, and what the anomalies",
    "among them were. That is history, and history does not change: nothing",
    "anybody does tomorrow can add a migration to yesterday. So this file is",
    "closed at a version and never needs refreshing.",
    "",
    "It deliberately does NOT record how many rows production holds. The first",
    "version of this file did, and the number was wrong within hours because",
    "another workstream applied a migration — a fact with a shelf life of",
    "minutes is not a safety invariant, and a test built on one teaches people",
    "to edit numbers until it passes.",
    "",
    "The invariant it supports: every repo migration at or below",
    "baselineThrough must appear in appliedVersions. A newer migration is",
    "ordinary work and is out of scope by construction.",
    "",
    "scripts/migration-baseline.mjs is the audit; tests/matrix/",
    "migrationHistory.test.mjs runs it against this repository and against",
    "synthetic drift. Regenerate ONLY as part of a fresh, deliberate",
    "reconciliation — never to make a test pass."
  ],
